For PaySame AND  PayMore corrected claims we will use a PLB segment to report the previously paid amounts.  

When we use the PLB segment we represent the SV03 and CLP04 values as the corrected claim amount without subtracting the previously paid amount, Then in the PLB segment we report the previously paid amount.  This allows us to take the CLP04 amount and subtract the PLB segment which would result in the BPR02 value represent what the additional payment would be or 0

For PayLess (Overpayments) - The corrected claim process reporting will use PLB segments to represent the Corrected Claim Payment.  This PLB amount will match the amount presented in the CLP04 element

As a reminder - BPR02 =CLP04-PLB
CLP04= sumofSVC03 segments
SVC03=SVC02 - CAS segments

For Overpayment transaction the PLB segment will be included in the 835 reporting and will represent the CORRECTED claim payment.

For PayMore, PaySame we will use the PLB segment representing the previously paid amounts 

When using the PLB method the SVC03 and CLP04 will not be reduced by the previously paid amounts (Prev paid amount is represented by the PLB)
